Article 3 Where a party applies for retrial, it shall submit to the People's Court a written application for retrial and provide copies in accordance with the number of the opposing parties.
The People's Court shall examine whether the written application for retrial contains the following matters:
(1) The basic information of the applicant for retrial and the opposing party, including names, domiciles, and effective contact methods; for a legal person or other organization, the name, domicile, and the name, position, and effective contact methods of its legal representative or principal responsible person;
(2) The name of the original trial People's Court and the case numbers of the original judgment, ruling, or mediation document;
(3) The statutory causes for applying for retrial and the specific facts and reasons;
(4) The specific requests for retrial.

Article 20 In any of the following circumstances, the original trial People's Court shall not be instructed to conduct a retrial:
(1) The original trial People's Court has no jurisdiction over the case;
(2) The adjudicators committed embezzlement or bribery, engaged in malpractices for personal gain, or rendered judgments in violation of law when trying the case;
(3) The original judgment or ruling was made after discussion by the adjudication committee of the original trial People's Court;
(4) Other circumstances where it is inappropriate to instruct the original trial People's Court to conduct a retrial.
